{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding","id":1079702,"title":"Less...intense ways of feeding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-17T00:01:37-07:00","id":1079702,"title":"Less...intense ways of feeding","content":"This is probably just from me being hilariously incompetent (or unwilling) at being a monster (I actually had to outsource to my other players in a Vampire game how to destroy someone to fulfill an Obsession condition), but I'm wondering what suggestions you guys have for feeding without it being totally harmful to someone. A Beast requires genuine fear and or pain to sustain themselves, if they don't have any relatives they can fulfill Family Dinner with, but surely there's some way of achieving that condition without requiring them to see a psychiatrist afterwards.<br /> <br /> My only method thus far is to have a Beast play someone genuinely scary in a stage production, a character that is terrifying yet once the play ends the Beast is able to go about the audience again. Even if that's relatively slim pickings for a Beast in terms of actual satiety, a good sized audience who buy into the performance should allow a production to at least give a decent meal.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that this kind of topic is kind of missing the point of Beast, but I like the idea of playing a decent person who has a very indecent hunger, and they manage to strike something of a tenuous compromise with it. Doubtless someone in the audience could be scarred by the strength of the performance, or it could derail the entire play if it's too strong, but...I dunno. It's been on my mind for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T01:54:46-07:00","id":1079724,"title":"","content":"The performance thing might be possible.<br /> <br /> I think the important thing here is to think first about what your Hunger is. Beasts don't all feed the same way, and defining what empowers your Beast is a big step towards figuring out ways to feed in minimally harmful ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, you can never completely avoid the potential of sending people to therapy, but a Nemesis that doxxes Twitter trolls probably doesn't do too much long term harm to the minds of said targets (even if this particular example isn't the best due to the distance unless the Nemesis focuses on doing it to nearby targets to observe the impact of their efforts)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T01:54:56-07:00","id":1079725,"title":"","content":"I've made a couple of characters that kinda do this.... one of them offers/runs a Tourist Trap Hotel that &quot;Guarantees&quot; you the most terrifying Nightmares. He's makes a point of it being consenual... Because people will pay for just about anything, especially big highs that come from being frightened/adrenaline from fear.<br /> (Seriously.. people have PAID to be Kidnapped.) He sees this as a Safer alternative to some of the more dangerous things people could do. Also one of the things he states is that you Will be Frightened.. not how. He's trying to get several other Beasts to come join his Hotel... The best way to get many people to feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 04-17-2017, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T02:15:39-07:00","id":1079726,"title":"","content":"First the easiest method is to keep yourself at low satiety. While this puts you are risk for your Horror lashing out if you don't feed, and you can't use nightmares as effectively, your Horror is less picky this gives you more wiggle room than you might have regardless of what your Horror's preferences are. For example a tyrant anakim might demand the utter cowing of an adversary, so at higher satiety the Horror might want want the utter breaking point to the extent of them collapsing or something like that. However at lower satiety you'd be justified in feeding off complete wins that aren't too horribly devestating to the person. Like a first to 10 one on one basketball game with the Beast performing an utter shut out to force the person to accept that they are that out classed. I mean it might upset the person a bit, but unless being the best at the game was absolutely essential to the person's psyche you're probably not doing much damage.<br /> <br /> Oh nemesis is also a good one if you're trying to run a good person. I mean the Horror might have it's interest in what it determines a crime and the appropriate punishment, but if you're into punishment then you can feed by handling crimes. God knows it's not that difficult for an Ugallu to figure out means providing evidence to the police of various criminal activities to enable to the Beast to feed on the arrests. (For the record dismantling criminal organizations is glorious for a ravager.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T02:48:52-07:00","id":1079730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1079725#post1079725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made a couple of characters that kinda do this.... one of them offers/runs a Tourist Trap Hotel that &quot;Guarantees&quot; you the most terrifying Nightmares. He's makes a point of it being consenual... Because people will pay for just about anything, especially big highs that come from being frightened/adrenaline from fear.<br /> (Seriously.. people have PAID to be Kidnapped.) He sees this as a Safer alternative to some of the more dangerous things people could do. Also one of the things he states is that you Will be Frightened.. not how. He's trying to get several other Beasts to come join his Hotel... The best way to get many people to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. This reminds me somewhat of Anteiku from Tokyo Ghoul. The 'ghouls' had no choice but to eat human flesh and many of them were really quite monstrous, but the ANteiku ghouls used the meat of suicides. It's not exactly the same thing, but it reminded me of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:49:40-07:00","id":1079868,"title":"","content":"My character, Hargrove, is a stage magician with a Horror that Hungers for Power, specifically for its victims to be utterly amazed by it. It wants to drive people insane, breaking down the lines between reality and fantasy, but it settles for the amazement and wonder that Hargrove invokes by making people truly believe. Your performance idea could work perfectly, provided that the fear is real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:07:52-07:00","id":1080110,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of nasty things that go bump in the night to easily supply worthy targets for Power Prey and Punishment hungers if running a vigilante would work for you. Prey explicitly allows sport hunting at low Satiety, and you could keep to population control, eat what you kill type behavior as much as possible. Hoard can be pretty manageable, depending on what you specifically collect. <br /> <br /> I have a game right now with a Ravager who mostly contents himself with graffiti and other small scale vandalism against The Man. When he goes bigger with his destruction it's in the form of things like burning down condemned buildings that the city refuses to renovate or tear down despite being a major health hazard. Scares the hell out of people but for a pretty good reason. <br /> <br /> Another Beast collects trophies, and throws herself into every competitive sport she can sign up for. In a pinch she'll take anything somebody is willing to bet on a contest of skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:33:19-07:00","id":1080343,"title":"","content":"So, like do these folks horrors whine about their choices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:54:00-07:00","id":1080464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1080343#post1080343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, like do these folks horrors whine about their choices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please your standard Horror only has the three settings. It's either in a food coma, complaining about being hungry, or eating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Eh for the most part if you're at low satiety then the horror is going to be upset due to being starving. As far as the feeding choices go if you're in the right ballpark that the Horror will eat then it should be fine most of the time, even if it views the food as not as good as it could be, of course there's always the possibility of failing a feeding roll in which case yeah the Horror has decided this particular feed is crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:16:47-07:00","id":1080478,"title":"","content":"My best advice is to think about what low trauma things a Beast can do to satiate their hunger while still providing good plot hooks for the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> A Makara Collecter I'm playing now steals magical secrets and artifacts either for hire or to keep them out of the hands of ordinary mortals who's lives could be destroyed by their power. In the former he hires himself out as a secret shopper to the local Mage Orders (primarily the Guardians of the Veil) in order to teach young Awakened the value of teamwork and cooperation. He leaves a warning for the cabal phantom thief style and gives them a timeframe of when he'll break into their Sanctum and steal a valuable item from each of them. If they can catch him or prevent him from stealing the items then they win and hopefully come away from that wiser. If he can steal their valuables then he wins and keeps them, hopefully showcasing what they did wrong in the process so when lives are really on the line they can properly work together. Although, if he wins he does get to keep their treasures. That is what's first agree'd upon when the cabal's mentor or Order hires him. <br /> <br /> This way the fear and loss are real, but it's done in a way that gives all of the chances in the world to the prey. Plus, if he does succeed then he'll have some very naive an pissed of Mages after him. Which is great. ^_^<br /> <br /> The other method is significantly easier since he's stealing from mortals and doesn't announce his presence like when he's on the clock. But there's a higher chance of collateral damage as while his point is to steal magical relics from mortals who don't know what they're getting into, there's always the off occasion that those mortals really do need those relics to either save themselves or their family from some supernatural threat they would be impossible to do otherwise. By stealing these relics the Beast tries to save them from the supernatural, but in doing so dooms them instead. Which I think is still good because the aftermath of such a mistake can lead to some fantastic story moments with the Beast trying to balance his Legend with his Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-18-2017, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:14:06-07:00","id":1081873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding#post1079702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate that this kind of topic is kind of missing the point of Beast, but I like the idea of playing a decent person who has a very indecent hunger, and they manage to strike something of a tenuous compromise with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all! This is very much in tune with Beast! There are even some examples in the core book, like the little girl pretending to drown (which, admittedly, would be very traumatic) or the secretary of the school's principal no one wanted to face.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head: Be the lawyer everyone is afraid of facing in court, because he always sees to it that justice wins (throw in some daredevil if you feel like it). The Ravager police chef who dismantles one crime syndicate after the other, through strategizing if not through being on the field himself. The Ugallu Nemesis mall security who notices EVERY thief, and lets them know before catching them.<br /> The Boxer who only wins against arrogant guys. The fellow student who leaves everyone else feel inadequate through his excellence.<br /> The security systems salesman who repeatedly breaks into rich homes to make them afraid - and stops once they have sufficiently secure homes.<br /> The old weirdo that is mean and scary to the kids - who keeps them safe from the other things that go bump in the night.<br /> How about an art collector, or curator, who presents scary artifacts from all over the world?<br /> Hell, why not a family-friendly version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1049309#post1049309\">Pickman</a>? Make an artist focused on creating scary art, you're bound to be able to feed a hungry Horror with that similar to your scary performer.<br /> <br /> You might want to stay away from Eshmaki Predators, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:33:41-07:00","id":1081880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1081873#post1081873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all! This is very much in tune with Beast! There are even some examples in the core book, like the little girl pretending to drown (which, admittedly, would be very traumatic) or the secretary of the school's principal no one wanted to face.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head: Be the lawyer everyone is afraid of facing in court, because he always sees to it that justice wins (throw in some daredevil if you feel like it). The Ravager police chef who dismantles one crime syndicate after the other, through strategizing if not through being on the field himself. The Ugallu Nemesis mall security who notices EVERY thief, and lets them know before catching them.<br /> The Boxer who only wins against arrogant guys. The fellow student who leaves everyone else feel inadequate through his excellence.<br /> The security systems salesman who repeatedly breaks into rich homes to make them afraid - and stops once they have sufficiently secure homes.<br /> The old weirdo that is mean and scary to the kids - who keeps them safe from the other things that go bump in the night.<br /> How about an art collector, or curator, who presents scary artifacts from all over the world?<br /> Hell, why not a family-friendly version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1049309#post1049309\">Pickman</a>? Make an artist focused on creating scary art, you're bound to be able to feed a hungry Horror with that similar to your scary performer.<br /> <br /> You might want to stay away from Eshmaki Predators, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see a Steven King book about the old crazy man in the neighborhood, in the spooky house, who terrifies the kids with stories, steals any bike or ball that ends up in his yard and so on.<br /> <br /> Then at the end, when the real terror has cornered the children, reveals himself as an even bigger boogeyman and axes the thing to death, saving the children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:39:14-07:00","id":1081884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1081880#post1081880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I could see a Steven King book about the old crazy man in the neighborhood, in the spooky house, who terrifies the kids with stories, steals any bike or ball that ends up in his yard and so on.<br /> <br /> Then at the end, when the real terror has cornered the children, reveals himself as an even bigger boogeyman and axes the thing to death, saving the children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigger boogeyman part aside, isnt that the plot of Monster House?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:47:58-07:00","id":1081885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1081884#post1081884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bigger boogeyman part aside, isnt that the plot of Monster House?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That movie was surprisingly dark and sad. Having to kill the remnant of your wife because she's too lost to her past of abuse to keep from being a threat to the neighbors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:21:31-07:00","id":1081957,"title":"","content":"@Wormwood<br /> <br /> Nice Pickman's Model reference. Honestly Pickman would make an excellent Beast template wholesale since he's also in the Dream Quest for Unknown Kadash. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-21-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:57:04-07:00","id":1081982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1081957#post1081957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Wormwood<br /> <br /> Nice Pickman's Model reference. Honestly Pickman would make an excellent Beast template wholesale since he's also in the Dream Quest for Unknown Kadash. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This is exactly why I have started my Lovecraft-inspired Beast Characters: You can turn a lot of his characters into Beasts pretty easily.<br /> As a a Bonus, I tried to mix the protagonists with the dominant monsters. So a ghoul for pickman, of course =D<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> The most important thing would probably be to chose your Hunger carefully. Tyrants can be pretty easy to satisfy without a fight: Check the Makara Tyrant sample character - all that taxi driver really does is letting people out in a 'scary' neighbourhood. Chances are, if picked correctly, this would scare them, but has little chance of causing lasting harm. (Unless you want to cause it, of course.) You could have someone that likes to collect blackmail-level information, lets people know he has it - and then does nothing with it. Just revels in his power. No 'harm' done, although the people certainly will experience degrees of fear.<br /> Throw in some Hacking skills if you want to stay anonymous. (Btw, Anonymous-style Hacker could be a fair concept of its own. Hack into a computer, leave a data-file saying 'Interesting stuff you have here. -yourstruly'. A private person will feel unhappy about that (especially so if there is sensitive data on the hard drive, e.g. corporation files). Federal institutations will be far more so. Harm done? None. Best case scenario, you improve their security systems and get to feed by showing off your l33t hax0r skills.<br /> <br /> There was also the sample character that basically made priests transgress their own rules, seducing them to sin, basically. Still pretty devastating, but nothing that couldn't be handled.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything that seemed helpful to you so far?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T03:28:30-07:00","id":1143427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1081982#post1081982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! This is exactly why I have started my Lovecraft-inspired Beast Characters: You can turn a lot of his characters into Beasts pretty easily.<br /> As a a Bonus, I tried to mix the protagonists with the dominant monsters. So a ghoul for pickman, of course =D<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> Throw in some Hacking skills if you want to stay anonymous. (Btw, Anonymous-style Hacker could be a fair concept of its own. Hack into a computer, leave a data-file saying 'Interesting stuff you have here. -yourstruly'. A private person will feel unhappy about that (especially so if there is sensitive data on the hard drive, e.g. corporation files). Federal institutations will be far more so. Harm done? None. Best case scenario, you improve their security systems and get to feed by showing off your l33t hax0r skills.<br /> <br /> There was also the sample character that basically made priests transgress their own rules, seducing them to sin, basically. Still pretty devastating, but nothing that couldn't be handled.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything that seemed helpful to you so far?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> There are some problems with that hacker idea: When a place has it's security compromised will likely fire whoever was originally in charge of security.<br /> <br /> Also, that Priest from the sample had a brood member who likes to take those vow breakers, dangle them off a bell tower and threaten to drop them if they don't renounce the church.<br /> <br /> ...Though, said fired security expert could then make a good potential antagonist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":".  Removed a line that was a bit too subjective. 09-24-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:47:11-07:00","id":1143508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1143427#post1143427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> There are some problems with that hacker idea: When a place has it's security compromised will likely fire whoever was originally in charge of security.<br /> <br /> Also, that Priest from the sample had a brood member who likes to take those vow breakers, dangle them off a bell tower and threaten to drop them if they don't renounce the church, so that guy really isn't to good<br /> <br /> ...Though, said fired security expert could then make a good potential antagonist...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit to not thinking that through completely (much as a Beast might stop at thinking 'no harm done, right?' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), and as I said in another thread, showing someone you have information about their misdeeds might have consequences, ranging from good (e.g. a couple talking out their problems; rare) to bad (e.g. overreact and break up in a nasty/accusatory way; probably more common) to catastrophic (e.g. someone becoming paranoid, dropping in work productivity and thus losing their job; uncommon?).<br /> Regarding the hacking: well, in most companies I know you'd only lose your job if the security breach was due to incompetency. If it was something like a zero day exploit or unknown method that was not easily prevented (without impeding running business), there is little anyone could have done against it, and if it was known, it is still not uncommon that the client takes a risk (e.g. following scenario: &quot;We found a security risk, shutting it would however impede x and y. We are working on a replacement for x and y that will not be affected by shutting the security risk down, however, that will take z days. Option a: we shut it down now, and take the fall in revenue resulting from not being able to do x and y properly. Option b: we keep it open while we work on the replacement, and hope for the best.&quot;. Taking b is more common than you might think.)<br /> <br /> That priest is not responsible for his brood member's actions, is he? (Trick question, of course he is since the two grouped up that way). What I really mean to say is: taking the concept priest without his broodmate makes him a far less intense form of feeding, which is basically what was asked for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, something completely different: You said &quot;that guy is not good&quot;. Of course not. No Beast is good. Applying human morality to a non-human entity is messed up in the first place, but black-and-white does not really fit into ChroD as a whole. Beasts feed by imposing their will on others without their consent, and while that can range from stressing people out to making them dread revision day, it can easily include violence and bodily harm. This is not to say that Beasts are necessary evil, though. You might dread revision day, but because you're scared so shitless of that, you don't procrastinate but work your ass off, develop amazing skills, motivate your people, and your guys make enormous earnings that year, getting nifty things like promotions and salary increases (or at least nice bonuses). A guy dies, but since he was head of a human trafficking ring and rapist, he won't really be missed. Neither of those things is good, or even okay, but we are more likely to accept them due to a perceived pay-off.<br /> All protagonists (to a degree even Hunters) are monsters. They transgress, violate and overstep social bounderies. What is okay to do, what is not okay to do does not apply to them, because their frame of reference is different, or so they claim. Some try to retain human morality, others dive into their monstrousness and justify what they do by some sort of &quot;That's natural&quot;.<br /> The truth is simply that they have an actual need they have to satisfy or face the consequences - even good intentions can pave the road to hell, whereas even an absolute asshole could do a lot of good by accident (Nice Job Fixing It Villian! is a Trope for a reason).<br /> In some games, and for some people, Feeding in an overt and obviously evil manner is fitting and called for. In others, you might want some more dubiosity. One way to make that possible is by introducing good intentions (Common with Nemesis going Punisher/DareDevil and the like), good consequences (You're a piece of work as a trainer and people are scared to death of you, but they keep coming because while you put them through hell in training, you also make them WIN) or less severe forms of feeding or a mixture of the above (e.g. the Ugallu that raises through the ranks of a Mega-Corp. Everyone competing is a scheming, manipulative asshole - and yet, it is you that will slowly rise to the top and take the power bit by bit. Because this is what you want: make them tremble before you, before, during and after you fought for the some position, just to let them know &quot;Yeah, I know you wanted it. I felt like taking it, though, so it is mine now. I could fire you for the shit you pulled, you know....? Kidding, kidding. Don't worry. I won't fire you. Yet.&quot;).<br /> <br /> I may have misread this (apologies in advance if I did), and I do not mean to come off as antagonizing (I often do, German works differently from English and makes me often sound rude online).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:43:20-07:00","id":1143569,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> No offense taken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I'm sorry if my own post offended you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1079725#post1079725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made a couple of characters that kinda do this.... one of them offers/runs a Tourist Trap Hotel that &quot;Guarantees&quot; you the most terrifying Nightmares. He's makes a point of it being consenual... Because people will pay for just about anything, especially big highs that come from being frightened/adrenaline from fear.<br /> (Seriously.. people have PAID to be Kidnapped.) He sees this as a Safer alternative to some of the more dangerous things people could do. Also one of the things he states is that you Will be Frightened.. not how. He's trying to get several other Beasts to come join his Hotel... The best way to get many people to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also imagine him letting Autumn Changeling work there, both to harvest glamour and to study the resultant dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1080478#post1080478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My best advice is to think about what low trauma things a Beast can do to satiate their hunger while still providing good plot hooks for the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> A Makara Collecter I'm playing now steals magical secrets and artifacts either for hire or to keep them out of the hands of ordinary mortals who's lives could be destroyed by their power. In the former he hires himself out as a secret shopper to the local Mage Orders (primarily the Guardians of the Veil) in order to teach young Awakened the value of teamwork and cooperation. He leaves a warning for the cabal phantom thief style and gives them a timeframe of when he'll break into their Sanctum and steal a valuable item from each of them. If they can catch him or prevent him from stealing the items then they win and hopefully come away from that wiser. If he can steal their valuables then he wins and keeps them, hopefully showcasing what they did wrong in the process so when lives are really on the line they can properly work together. Although, if he wins he does get to keep their treasures. That is what's first agree'd upon when the cabal's mentor or Order hires him.<br /> <br /> This way the fear and loss are real, but it's done in a way that gives all of the chances in the world to the prey. Plus, if he does succeed then he'll have some very naive an pissed of Mages after him. Which is great. ^_^<br /> <br /> The other method is significantly easier since he's stealing from mortals and doesn't announce his presence like when he's on the clock. But there's a higher chance of collateral damage as while his point is to steal magical relics from mortals who don't know what they're getting into, there's always the off occasion that those mortals really do need those relics to either save themselves or their family from some supernatural threat they would be impossible to do otherwise. By stealing these relics the Beast tries to save them from the supernatural, but in doing so dooms them instead. Which I think is still good because the aftermath of such a mistake can lead to some fantastic story moments with the Beast trying to balance his Legend with his Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bet this guy butts heads with the AKD quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:58:02-07:00","id":1143574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1143569#post1143569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> No offense taken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I'm sorry if my own post offended you.<br /> I could also imagine him letting Autumn Changeling work there, both to harvest glamour and to study the resultant dreams.<br /> Bet this guy butts heads with the AKD quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, not at all =)<br /> <br /> What is the AKD? Agnis Kai Doru? If so, yes, I agree. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> I can also see the Collector piss off a Mummy's cult by taking their relics, which is NEVER a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:26:07-07:00","id":1143883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1079726#post1079726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First the easiest method is to keep yourself at low satiety. While this puts you are risk for your Horror lashing out if you don't feed, and you can't use nightmares as effectively, your Horror is less picky this gives you more wiggle room than you might have regardless of what your Horror's preferences are. For example a tyrant anakim might demand the utter cowing of an adversary, so at higher satiety the Horror might want want the utter breaking point to the extent of them collapsing or something like that. However at lower satiety you'd be justified in feeding off complete wins that aren't too horribly devestating to the person. Like a first to 10 one on one basketball game with the Beast performing an utter shut out to force the person to accept that they are that out classed. I mean it might upset the person a bit, but unless being the best at the game was absolutely essential to the person's psyche you're probably not doing much damage.<br /> <br /> Oh nemesis is also a good one if you're trying to run a good person. I mean the Horror might have it's interest in what it determines a crime and the appropriate punishment, but if you're into punishment then you can feed by handling crimes. God knows it's not that difficult for an Ugallu to figure out means providing evidence to the police of various criminal activities to enable to the Beast to feed on the arrests. (For the record dismantling criminal organizations is glorious for a ravager.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how my Namtaru Nemesis feeds. He basically acts as a vigilante crimefighter who targets the worst criminals in his city. He's also a psychiatrist who works at an asylum. Inspired by various Batman villains, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T14:03:30-07:00","id":1143892,"title":"","content":"Why vigilante, though? A judge, a jailer, a sheriff, a lawyer... they all can work within the legal systems of our society and still manage to feed. Hell, for what it's worth, an Ugallu Nemesis (or Ravagers) could easily work as an investigative reporter who uncovers dirty secrets of corrupt politicians/CEOs/Corporative practises/dirty cops/illegal activities of club owners etc. and feed this way. With any combination of 5 Atavisms he'd be set to rule this domain (Needs Must, Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song). 2 of those would be starting Atavisms, and buying one or up to three more isn't too hard.<br /> <br /> You could have bounty hunters, military drill sergeants, boxers (seriously, why don't martial artists come up more often here?) or other athletes.<br /> Hell, you <i>could </i>even have a Beast that feeds through owning competitions like quiz shows, dancing, cooking, whathaveyou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T15:05:52-07:00","id":1143908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1143892#post1143892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why vigilante, though? A judge, a jailer, a sheriff, a lawyer... they all can work within the legal systems of our society and still manage to feed. Hell, for what it's worth, an Ugallu Nemesis (or Ravagers) could easily work as an investigative reporter who uncovers dirty secrets of corrupt politicians/CEOs/Corporative practises/dirty cops/illegal activities of club owners etc. and feed this way. With any combination of 5 Atavisms he'd be set to rule this domain (Needs Must, Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song). 2 of those would be starting Atavisms, and buying one or up to three more isn't too hard.<br /> <br /> You could have bounty hunters, military drill sergeants, boxers (seriously, why don't martial artists come up more often here?) or other athletes.<br /> Hell, you <i>could </i>even have a Beast that feeds through owning competitions like quiz shows, dancing, cooking, whathaveyou.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mainly because the city he lives in has no shortage of individuals who need a double-dose of bloody justice. Also because I've always wanted to play a vigilante hero in the WoD but i never liked Hunters because they tend to be largely ignorant of things and just aren't scary enough to have the impact of a good, nightmarish beats. I almost made his horror a giant, shadowy bat monster rather than the mad doctor he ended up being. It was super hard to avoid taking Wings of the Raptor and From the Shadows and going 'I AM THE NIGHT' every time he swooped down on an evildoer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically it wasn't about easy; personality-wise its the kind of character who is probably too altruistic for his own good. He adopted a teenaged girl off the streets and makes a habit of roughing up the local crooks in his city's worst neighborhood every other night or so. They are starting to <i>fear </i>the seemingly-unkillable man in the white mask who appears out of nowhere and puts an end to anyone who can't stop breaking the law and victimizing those less fortunate and always knows when you are lying (He has Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul, Mimir's Wisdom, Infestation and Basilisk's Touch). I'm actually trying to have him become the Apex, though we'll see how that works out in the long-term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:45:53-07:00","id":1144189,"title":"","content":"Just realized that a surgeon could easily cause a lot of fear, teach people lessons and still effectively do some good a la House...<br /> Thing is, Atavisms and Nightmares do not present themselves much for that line of work (no dex-improving abilities, outside of Mimir's Wisdom not really much that could help with this kind of thing)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16101_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16101\" data-vbnamecard=\"16101\">Eternal Darkness</a> <br /> sounds good to me. Also very tanky dude, with 2 out of the 5 Atavisms for the ultimate tank. Mimir's wisdom is a nice touch. The approach might work well in spreading the legend, too. So apex is easier to achieve.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T15:15:42-07:00","id":1144214,"title":"","content":"The answer to this question is less about how the player feels towards the feeding method, and more about what kind of character they're trying to play. Some Beasts need to hurt people in order to sustain themselves, that's just how they are. But that doesn't mean that every Beast has to do it, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only Hungers that have a frequent need to engage in physical violence is Prey and Ruin. The others might use it as a last resort, or when they're too desperate to come up with an intricate performance and just need a quick meal. So there are ways to you can go about imparting lessons without having to actually hurt people on the physical level.<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the process is supposed to be intense. Beasts feed on the terror of their victims, and the most rewarding meals come from when the victim learns something from the experience. It's not required, but teaching the victim a valuable lesson helps prevent the Beast from becoming an unrepentant psychopath. Jump scare tactics aren't going to be imparting any deep wisdom upon the victims, especially in recent years where the horror genre is saturated in that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> You need a scare that shakes them on a personal level, so that they reflect upon their situation and learn how to improve themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T06:34:28-07:00","id":1144371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1079725#post1079725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made a couple of characters that kinda do this.... one of them offers/runs a Tourist Trap Hotel that &quot;Guarantees&quot; you the most terrifying Nightmares. He's makes a point of it being consenual... Because people will pay for just about anything, especially big highs that come from being frightened/adrenaline from fear.<br /> (Seriously.. people have PAID to be Kidnapped.) He sees this as a Safer alternative to some of the more dangerous things people could do. Also one of the things he states is that you Will be Frightened.. not how. He's trying to get several other Beasts to come join his Hotel... The best way to get many people to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are haunted house attractions in America that require you to sign a legal waver before they let you participate. These attractions last up to 18 hours and are specifically designed to reenact both physical and psychological torture. And because of the legally binding waver you just signed, the ride only ends when you get through the whole thing, or when you become medically unable to continue and need to be rushed to the hospital!<br /> <br /> Yeah, people know this shit exists, and they pay for it, regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:28:22-07:00","id":1144397,"title":"","content":"How could a Collector feed from this Haunted House?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:49:59-07:00","id":1144487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1144397#post1144397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could a Collector feed from this Haunted House?</div> </div> </div> </div>Photos, locks of hair, their left sock. Collectors have the downside of always being more specific than other feeding types even at lower satiety, but you can probably figure a way to make it work. Hell depending on the place and the hoard you could potentially keep your collection right in the open to freak people out worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T00:30:04-07:00","id":1144663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1144487#post1144487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Photos, locks of hair, their left sock. Collectors have the downside of always being more specific than other feeding types even at lower satiety, but you can probably figure a way to make it work. Hell depending on the place and the hoard you could potentially keep your collection right in the open to freak people out worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those would work better as trophies for a Tyrant or Predator imo. Collectors are supposed to take something away that you value Highly, the disappearence of which makes you rethink your priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T11:07:00-07:00","id":1144846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079702-less-intense-ways-of-feeding?p=1144663#post1144663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those would work better as trophies for a Tyrant or Predator imo. Collectors are supposed to take something away that you value Highly, the disappearence of which makes you rethink your priorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Collector in this sitituation would probably collect something more.. Conceptual. The Physical Item they take would be different each time.. but it's a representation of taking something else from them. &quot;Delusions of Grandeur&quot; could be a pocket watch that the person earned from an awards ceremony for their job. &quot;Hope for the future/Idealism&quot; could be a piece of their hair (Or all of their Hair if they are a Model...) or something else of that ilk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T11:20:26-07:00","id":1144858,"title":"","content":"Some people actually are really big on their hair, so cutting part of it would potentially work based on the person. Photos it varies since taking a photo of the person might not; you've got a decent shot if you were to take a photo from their phone and delete the one there; and depending on what the photo is of you've got a good chance since blackmail exists for a reason. The sock wouldn't normally be one, but depending on what you're allowed to do to a person in these circumstances the sock could actually become important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T11:35:00-07:00","id":1144865,"title":"","content":"Taking the whole phone might work really well. Not only are those pretty expensive these days (up to the price of a fully-staffed gaming pc), they also contain important and valuable data, as you mentioned (photos, numbers, passwords....) and to some people, their phones are more important than to others (those to whom the phone is basically the lifeline of communication - shutting people that spend many hours on social networks - like this forum, ironically- actually has mental effects akin to isolation. Which is scary).<br /> <br /> Yeah, people that are very focused on their appearance or even vain are more likely to be thrown off by you taking a minor accessory, as their appearance is something they carefully cultivate and chose. You taking their stuff threatens their identity.<br /> <br /> In addition, taking something like earings, rings, necklaces or any other item they carry has the chance of it being a heirloom or similar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, a nice collector lets the people panic over their lost possession, but gives it back when they ask in the lost&amp;found. As per core:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you truly own nothing but what you can carry at a dead run, the Collector forces her target to choose what to pick up before the running even starts. Some Collectors let it go at that. Cruel Beasts chase down the target and take his prize anyway. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T02:03:18-07:00","id":1148248,"title":"","content":"One example of how an Eshmaki or Ugallu might feed <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentN